<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Instruction of Amenemhat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Instruction of Amenemhat is an ancient Egyptian literary text of the Twelfth Dynasty in which the dead king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenemhat-i">Amenemhat I</a> advises his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-i">Senusret I</a>, describing an attack on his life by members of his court. Probably composed early in Senusret's reign, it supported his rule and warned against trusting others. It was much copied by scribes in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/instruction-of-amenemhat.jpg" alt="Instruction of Amenemhat" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: rowanwindwhistler · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facs%C3%ADmilLasInstruccionesDelReyAmenemhatI_(46149914632)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
